    "resource": {
      "url": "https://api.bitrefill.com/x402/connect",
      "description": "Authenticate by signing the sign-in-with-x challenge with the SAME wallet that paid the invoice. Steps: (1) read the challenge fields from this 402 response's extensions[\"sign-in-with-x\"].info (domain, uri, version, chainId, nonce, issuedAt, expirationTime, statement); (2) build the CAIP-122/EIP-4361 (SIWE) message from them and sign it with your wallet (eip191 personal_sign; smart wallets / EIP-1271 + EIP-6492 are supported); (3) base64-encode a JSON object of the DECOMPOSED fields { domain, address, uri, version, chainId, type: \"eip191\", nonce, issuedAt, signature } (NOT { message, signature }) and send it in the SIGN-IN-WITH-X request header, then retry. The @x402/extensions sign-in-with-x client (createSIWxClientHook) builds this header for you; pin it to the version the challenge advertises to avoid header-shape drift. Tip: sign this same challenge once at POST /x402/connect to mint a reusable access token; send it as the X-Access-Token: <token> request header to skip both the fee and re-signing on every route until it expires. The one exception is invoice/pay: the token does nothing there — it settles the invoice's real USDC, and the wallet that sends that payment is the payer.",
      "mimeType": ""
    },
